DevOps Interview Command Series — Splunk (Day 16) 🔎

Splunk is a log analytics & observability powerhouse.
From incident investigation to security monitoring and RCA, Splunk is heavily used by DevOps, SRE, and Ops teams.

If you’re preparing for DevOps / SRE / Cloud interviews, these are the Splunk commands & searches you must know:

splunk --version

systemctl start splunk
systemctl status splunk
systemctl restart splunk

/opt/splunk/bin/splunk status
/opt/splunk/bin/splunk start
/opt/splunk/bin/splunk stop

index=_internal
index=_internal | head 10
index=main | stats count
index=main | sort - _time

index=main error
index=main | search error OR failed
index=main | stats count by host
index=main | timechart count

index=main | rex "errorCode=(?<code>\d+)"
index=main | stats count by code

index=main | top source
index=main | rare source

🎯 Interview Focus
• Logs vs metrics vs traces
• Indexes, sourcetypes & events
• Searching & filtering logs efficiently
• Dashboards & alerts basics
• Troubleshooting production issues using logs
• Splunk vs ELK comparison
